{"type": "say", "text": "Thanks, Marisol, and thanks everyone for the thoughtful flags already. Let me walk you through the proposal from the ERG side. The motivation here is practical: Mosaic and Bridge have seen significant overlap in membership and programming themes over the past year. We've been coordinating informally on several events, and the idea emerged that rather than duplicating efforts, we could combine our monthly programming under one shared charter — pooling resources, reducing scheduling conflicts for shared members, and creating a more cohesive community experience. Under the proposed structure, we'd maintain a single monthly meeting instead of two separate ones, with co-facilitated leadership drawing from both existing leadership groups. The shared charter would outline programming goals, governance, and decision-making processes. We'd consolidate the mailing lists so communications go through one channel. That said, I want to be transparent that there's an important commitment I made to Mosaic members that I need to put on the table formally now. I promised them — in a group meeting, though it wasn't added to the written proposal — that I would only support a merger if members received a written charter and the arrangement had a formal review after exactly 90 days. I want to make sure that commitment is part of this consultation."}
```

